+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>Visualize top genes in principal components</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo0LCJzaXplX2JlaGF2aW9yIjoxLCJ3aWR0aCI6OH0= -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>Later on (in FindClusters and TSNE) you will pick a number of principal components to use. This has the effect of keeping the major directions of variation in the data and, ideally, supressing noise. There is no correct answer to the number to use, but a decent rule of thumb is to go until the plot plateaus.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuUENFbGJvd1Bsb3Qob2JqZWN0ID0gdGlzcylcbmBgYCJ9 -->
+<pre class="r"><code>PCElbowPlot(object = tiss)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0IjozNzQuNTM2NSwic2l6ZV9iZWhhdmlvciI6MCwid2lkdGgiOjYwNn0= -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>Choose the number of principal components to use.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuIyBTZXQgbnVtYmVyIG9mIHByaW5jaXBhbCBjb21wb25lbnRzLiBcbm4ucGNzID0gMTVcbmBgYCJ9 -->
+<pre class="r"><code># Set number of principal components. 
+n.pcs = 15</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>The clustering is performed based on a nearest neighbors graph. Cells that have similar expression will be joined together. The Louvain algorithm looks for groups of cells with high modularity–more connections within the group than between groups. The resolution parameter determines the scale. Higher resolution will give more clusters, lower resolution will give fewer.</p>
+<p>For the top-level clustering, aim to under-cluster instead of over-cluster. It will be easy to subset groups and further analyze them below.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuIyBTZXQgcmVzb2x1dGlvbiBcbnJlcy51c2VkIDwtIDFcbnRpc3MgPC0gRmluZENsdXN0ZXJzKG9iamVjdCA9IHRpc3MsIHJlZHVjdGlvbi50eXBlID0gXCJwY2FcIiwgZGltcy51c2UgPSAxOm4ucGNzLCBcbiAgICByZXNvbHV0aW9uID0gcmVzLnVzZWQsIHByaW50Lm91dHB1dCA9IDAsIHNhdmUuU05OID0gVFJVRSlcbmBgYCJ9 -->
+<pre class="r"><code># Set resolution 
+res.used &lt;- 1
+tiss &lt;- FindClusters(object = tiss, reduction.type = &quot;pca&quot;, dims.use = 1:n.pcs, 
+    resolution = res.used, print.output = 0, save.SNN = TRUE)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-output-begin  -->
+<pre><code>Build parameters exactly match those of already computed and stored SNN. To force recalculation, set force.recalc to TRUE.Clustering parameters for resolution 1 exactly match those of already computed. 
+  To force recalculation, set force.recalc to TRUE.</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-output-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>We use TSNE solely to visualize the data.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin  -->
+<pre class="r"><code># If cells are too spread out, you can raise the perplexity. If you have few cells, try a lower perplexity (but never less than 10).
+tiss &lt;- RunTSNE(object = tiss, dims.use = 1:n.pcs, seed.use = 10, perplexity=30)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuVFNORVBsb3Qob2JqZWN0ID0gdGlzcywgZG8ubGFiZWwgPSBULCBwdC5zaXplID0gMS4yLCBsYWJlbC5zaXplID0gNClcbmBgYCJ9 -->
+<pre class="r"><code>TSNEPlot(object = tiss, do.label = T, pt.size = 1.2, label.size = 4)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0IjoyOTcuMjgwNiwic2l6ZV9iZWhhdmlvciI6MCwid2lkdGgiOjQ4MX0= -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuZ2VuZXNfdG9fY2hlY2sgPSBjKCdNeWY1JywgJ015b2QxJywgJ1BkZ2ZyYScsICdBdHhuMScsICdQZWNhbTEnLCdQdHByYycsJ0l0Z2FtJywnQ2QzZycsJ0NkNCcsICdDZDE5JywgJ0NoYWQnLCdDaG9kbCcsICdTb3g5JywgJ0FjYW4nLCdBY3RhMicpXG5gYGAifQ== -->
+<pre class="r"><code>genes_to_check = c('Myf5', 'Myod1', 'Pdgfra', 'Atxn1', 'Pecam1','Ptprc','Itgam','Cd3g','Cd4', 'Cd19', 'Chad','Chodl', 'Sox9', 'Acan','Acta2')</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo0LCJzaXplX2JlaGF2aW9yIjoxLCJ3aWR0aCI6MTJ9 -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64,[REDACTED_AWS_FOR_PUBLIC_RELEASE][REDACTED_AWS_FOR_PUBLIC_RELEASE]" /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>Dotplots let you see the intensity of exppression and the fraction of cells expressing for each of your genes of interest. The radius shows you the percent of cells in that cluster with at least one read sequenced from that gene. The color level indicates the average Z-score of gene expression for cells in that cluster, where the scaling is done over taken over all cells in the sample.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo4LCJzaXplX2JlaGF2aW9yIjoxLCJ3aWR0aCI6MTB9 -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo4LCJzaXplX2JlaGF2aW9yIjoxLCJ3aWR0aCI6MTB9 -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin eyJkYXRhIjoiYGBgclxuVmxuUGxvdCh0aXNzLCBcIk15ZjVcIiwgdXNlLnJhdz0gVCwgbkNvbCA9IDIpXG5gYGAifQ== -->
+<pre class="r"><code>VlnPlot(tiss, &quot;Myf5&quot;, use.raw= T, nCol = 2)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-plot-begin eyJjb25kaXRpb25zIjpbXSwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo4LCJzaXplX2JlaGF2aW9yIjoxLCJ3aWR0aCI6OH0= -->
+<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p>
+<!-- rnb-plot-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>We can also find all differentially expressed genes marking each cluster. This may take some time.</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin  -->
+<pre class="r"><code>#clust.markers0 &lt;- FindMarkers(object = tiss, ident.1 = 0, only.pos = TRUE, min.pct = 0.25, thresh.use = 0.25)
+#tiss.markers &lt;- FindAllMarkers(object = tiss, only.pos = TRUE, min.pct = 0.25, thresh.use = 0.25)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-end -->
+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<p>Display the top markers you computed above.</p>
